      <Docs>
        <summary>
            Gets or sets the retry budget options.
            </summary>
        <value>
            The default value is <see langword="null" />, which means retries are not limited by a budget.
            </value>
        <remarks>
            The budget is applied by the standard resilience handler and by
            <see cref="M:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryResiliencePipelineBuilderExtensions.AddRetryWithBudget(Polly.ResiliencePipelineBuilder{System.Net.Http.HttpResponseMessage},Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryStrategyOptions)" />.
            <see cref="M:Polly.RetryResiliencePipelineBuilderExtensions.AddRetry``1(Polly.ResiliencePipelineBuilder{``0},Polly.Retry.RetryStrategyOptions{``0})" />
            can't apply the budget, so it throws a <see cref="T:System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException" /> when the budget is set, instead of ignoring it.
            See <see cref="T:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions" /> for more details.
            </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
